  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASEED Food Activist Lab</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">10-15 aspiring activists will attend four days of workshops, networking, project planning, andfarming as an introduction to food systems activism in Amsterdam and beyond. ASEED willprovide insight into the three main topics of our own work: corporate control, localagroecological alternatives, and international solidarity. Meaning what we fight against, what wefight for, and who we fight with.ASEED has many years of experience in training young change makers to take action totransform our food system. We support them in obtaining skills and confidence to become moreexperienced campaigners within the topic of sustainable food systems. Good internal processesand work flow form a sound basis for activist projects, and this is why we will also emphasizegaining organisational skills such as anti- oppression, regeneration and well-being.This Activist Lab programme with have a boot-camp format and take place at ADM Noord/HetGroene Veld outside Amsterdam, a location close to the city with easy access from the citycentre. During the four days of Activist Lab sessions, participants will receive guidance onforming their own individual or collaborative projects related to food systems in or outside theNetherlands. This intensive training structure will provide an immersive experience, whereparticipants will also learn collective processes, get to know each other, and dive deep into theirprojects without distractions. On the final day in Amsterdam, participants will present andimplement their projects.</narrative>
  </description>
